Acceptance criteria:
  Public runtime includes the qualified calmer interface, Education navigation,
    six-specialization/online-course/entry-rule improvements and complete
    initially-Planned Godot-first mission. No genuine work is inferred.
  README and living guides describe the current product accurately while
    retaining the approved illustrations and their honest source scope.
  Publish only reviewed public-safe source/docs/tracking. Private reports,
    screenshots, PDFs, context stores, browser records and credentials remain
    excluded. Preserve the existing narrow approved academic product preset.
  Verify Zanark account/repository/transport and both effective identities;
    keep current required trailers. Do not change global auth or rewrite history.
  Reuse the existing main-branch Pages workflow and minimum permissions;
    no new scheduler, secret provisioning, public service or unrelated trigger.
  Exact authorized SHA/run must succeed and the actual hosted bytes/controls
    must match its artifact. Preserve failures and distinguish local, hosted,
    human acceptance and any documentation-only follow-through.
  Keep the original issue/Project/item identities and Kanban layout. Private
    document workstreams are not permission to publish their report bodies.
  Preserve both original local previews and the owner's actual browser data;
    qualification uses disposable contexts and only owned temporary helpers.

